<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Dashboard</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <nav>
      <a href="/dashboard" class="active">Dashboard</a>
      <a href="/profile">Profile</a>
      <form action="/logout" method="POST" class="logout-form">
        <button type="submit" class="link-button">Logout</button>
      </form>
    </nav>

    <h1>Dashboard</h1>
    <p>Welcome back, <strong><%= user.username %></strong>. This is a protected route — you can only see it while logged in.</p>

    <div class="info-box">
      <p><strong>Session ID:</strong> <%= sessionId %></p>
      <p>This session is stored in Redis (key <code>sess:&lt;sessionId&gt;</code>), not in server memory — so it works even across multiple app instances.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
